WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.287 --> 00:00:08.387
.

00:00:08.554 --> 00:00:13.125
&gt;&gt;&gt; Tonight exodus at last, some

00:00:13.258 --> 00:00:13.792
70,000 people who have been

00:00:14.126 --> 00:00:14.493
stuck at burning man are now

00:00:14.593 --> 00:00:16.695
slowly being allowed to leave.

00:00:17.129 --> 00:00:20.132
You are looking here at live

00:00:20.165 --> 00:00:20.766
pictures of this massive caravan

00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:22.267
of festival Goers making their

00:00:22.401 --> 00:00:23.669
way out of the desert.

00:00:23.802 --> 00:00:25.471
Rain turned the normally dry

00:00:25.604 --> 00:00:26.505
Nevada lake bed where the

00:00:26.672 --> 00:00:30.142
festival is held into a sticky, muddy mess shutting down the

00:00:30.209 --> 00:00:32.144
only road in or out, stranding

00:00:32.144 --> 00:00:33.212
people for days.

00:00:33.312 --> 00:00:36.648
Nick watt is out front.

00:00:36.815 --> 00:00:38.384
&gt;&gt; Reporter: The exodus

00:00:38.484 --> 00:00:40.185
underway, that sunshine you see

00:00:40.352 --> 00:00:42.454
is the savior drying the mud

00:00:42.588 --> 00:00:44.790
just enough for tires to grip,

00:00:45.157 --> 00:00:46.558
not sink into sludge.

00:00:46.692 --> 00:00:47.793
&gt;&gt; It was impossible to

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:49.161
function, impossible to move

00:00:49.194 --> 00:00:51.163
around, a lot of struggling

00:00:51.163 --> 00:00:52.664
people in what became very cold,

00:00:52.798 --> 00:00:54.466
very storm-like conditions.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:57.169
People's tents and the entire

00:00:57.169 --> 00:00:59.171
camps became pretty much

00:00:59.171 --> 00:00:59.271
destroyed.

00:00:59.405 --> 00:01:00.172
&gt;&gt; Reporter: More than 70,000

00:01:00.172 --> 00:01:05.444
people were basically trapped

00:01:05.544 --> 00:01:06.178
for days.

00:01:06.178 --> 00:01:08.180
Trapped in this makeshift desert

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:12.184
city that pops up in Nevada

00:01:12.184 --> 00:01:12.551
every year around labor day

00:01:12.684 --> 00:01:16.188
filled with campers and kroet

00:01:16.188 --> 00:01:17.456
creators, fun lovers and those

00:01:17.556 --> 00:01:19.691
with their freak flag flying,

00:01:19.792 --> 00:01:21.226
that culminates in the man

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:21.560
burning.

00:01:21.727 --> 00:01:23.629
&gt;&gt; We planned on leaving right

00:01:23.762 --> 00:01:24.630
after the man burned, which is

00:01:24.763 --> 00:01:26.198
Saturday night, and then it

00:01:26.198 --> 00:01:27.232
started raining on us.

00:01:27.399 --> 00:01:28.834
Everybody took their shoes off,

00:01:29.201 --> 00:01:30.202
started dancing in the mud.

00:01:30.202 --> 00:01:31.303
It was great, and then the

00:01:31.403 --> 00:01:33.205
reality sunk in that we couldn't

00:01:33.305 --> 00:01:33.505
leave.

00:01:33.672 --> 00:01:34.506
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Chris rock and some

00:01:34.673 --> 00:01:36.408
other celebs decided to take the

00:01:36.508 --> 00:01:39.645
only uncomfortable exit

00:01:39.745 --> 00:01:40.212
available.

00:01:40.212 --> 00:01:41.447
&gt;&gt; We just got up and started

00:01:41.613 --> 00:01:42.648
walking, and we walked about

00:01:42.781 --> 00:01:45.250
three hours in the mud, and he

00:01:45.384 --> 00:01:45.851
was happy.

00:01:46.218 --> 00:01:47.853
It was me, I think Cindy

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:50.856
Crawford walked with us, Kaia

00:01:51.223 --> 00:01:53.225
Gerber, Austin butler, it was a

00:01:53.258 --> 00:01:54.259
challenge, but it was honestly

00:01:54.426 --> 00:01:55.527
one of the highlights of the

00:01:55.661 --> 00:01:57.229
whole trip.

00:01:57.262 --> 00:01:59.865
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Many embracing the

00:02:00.232 --> 00:02:03.235
ethos of self-reliance.

00:02:03.235 --> 00:02:05.237
&gt;&gt; I was waiting for the

00:02:05.304 --> 00:02:06.238
looting, honestly.

00:02:06.238 --> 00:02:07.239
It's really beautiful actually

00:02:07.372 --> 00:02:09.408
when you go into the camps,

00:02:09.508 --> 00:02:11.243
everybody was helping each other

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:11.477
out.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:12.811
&gt;&gt; Burning man, raining man,

00:02:13.245 --> 00:02:13.812
suck it up.

00:02:14.246 --> 00:02:14.713
Stick it out.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:17.249
&gt;&gt; I had my rv here and all my

00:02:17.249 --> 00:02:19.251
other camp mates have rvs or big

00:02:19.251 --> 00:02:20.586
rental trucks or things like

00:02:20.719 --> 00:02:22.354
that, and getting those out was

00:02:22.521 --> 00:02:23.255
basically impossible.

00:02:23.255 --> 00:02:24.256
Sure, you could have walked out.

00:02:24.356 --> 00:02:26.758
What am I going tad with all my

00:02:26.859 --> 00:02:27.259
stuff.

00:02:27.259 --> 00:02:28.460
&gt;&gt; Reporter: All this Chao

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:29.828
caused by less than an inch of

00:02:30.262 --> 00:02:31.262
rain.

00:02:30.262 --> 00:02:33.265
&gt;&gt; Even just the slightest bit

00:02:33.365 --> 00:02:35.267
of rain makes everything super

00:02:35.267 --> 00:02:35.467
slick.

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:37.269
You have like five pounds of mud

00:02:37.369 --> 00:02:37.669
on your feet.

00:02:37.836 --> 00:02:39.371
&gt;&gt; This is a desert, nothing

00:02:39.538 --> 00:02:42.274
much grows, she soil isn't

00:02:42.441 --> 00:02:43.742
lovely and absorbent, it's just

00:02:43.909 --> 00:02:44.576
miles of gray clay.

00:02:44.676 --> 00:02:46.478
Most years this is a dusty, not

00:02:47.279 --> 00:02:48.747
a muddy mess.

00:02:48.847 --> 00:02:50.349
And under an inch of rain, well,

00:02:50.449 --> 00:02:52.284
that's still two or three

00:02:52.351 --> 00:02:56.288
months' worth of rain in this

00:02:56.421 --> 00:02:58.824
arid land within just 24 hours.

00:02:58.957 --> 00:03:00.359
Tonight they will finally burn

00:03:00.526 --> 00:03:01.960
the man for those that remain

00:03:02.294 --> 00:03:09.301
and pray for no rain.

00:03:09.301 --> 00:03:11.303
So at noon today, organizers

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:12.471
said there were still about

00:03:12.638 --> 00:03:14.573
64,000 people on the site.

00:03:14.673 --> 00:03:15.374
Two hours later they officially

00:03:15.541 --> 00:03:16.441
opened the road.

00:03:16.575 --> 00:03:18.310
But they are advising people

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:19.678
maybe you want to wait until

00:03:19.845 --> 00:03:21.313
tomorrow, but by the look of

00:03:21.346 --> 00:03:23.682
those lines, not many people are

00:03:23.782 --> 00:03:25.651
taking that advice.

00:03:25.784 --> 00:03:27.319
Listen, radical self-reliance,

00:03:27.319 --> 00:03:29.855
that's what they say is one of

00:03:29.988 --> 00:03:34.326
the central ethos of this

00:03:34.326 --> 00:03:35.327
festival, this year proved why.

00:03:35.327 --> 00:03:35.494
Briana.

00:03:35.661 --> 00:03:37.796
&gt;&gt; Sure did, Nick watt, thank

00:03:37.963 --> 00:03:39.865
you.

00:03:39.998 --> 00:03:41.967
&gt;&gt; And out front now is caz who

00:03:42.334 --> 00:03:44.336
is still at burning man.

00:03:44.336 --> 00:03:44.703
We are looking.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:45.704
We have some video, actually,

00:03:45.804 --> 00:03:48.574
that you sent us of just some

00:03:48.707 --> 00:03:51.343
incredibly thick mud and soaking

00:03:51.343 --> 00:03:51.877
wet tents.

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:53.912
What has it been like for you

00:03:54.346 --> 00:03:57.616
all living in these conditions?

00:03:57.716 --> 00:04:01.920
&gt;&gt; Actually, you know, we have a

00:04:02.354 --> 00:04:03.355
really well-organized camp, camp

00:04:03.355 --> 00:04:05.624
daydream, and half the camp is

00:04:05.791 --> 00:04:09.361
rvs, and half the camp is tents,

00:04:09.428 --> 00:04:12.998
so as soon as the tents started

00:04:13.365 --> 00:04:14.800
getting water logged or

00:04:14.933 --> 00:04:16.635
unlivable, people in rvs started

00:04:16.802 --> 00:04:18.503
taking in some of the tenters so

00:04:18.637 --> 00:04:20.739
everybody was warm.

00:04:20.906 --> 00:04:22.374
We also have shipping

00:04:22.374 --> 00:04:24.376
containers, semitrucks that we

00:04:24.376 --> 00:04:28.914
had emptied out and we made

00:04:29.047 --> 00:04:30.649
really beautiful lounges in

00:04:30.816 --> 00:04:31.850
there for people to sleep in,

00:04:32.017 --> 00:04:33.852
blankets, you know, we are a

00:04:34.386 --> 00:04:36.388
community that comes together in

00:04:36.421 --> 00:04:38.957
hard times, so this actually

00:04:39.391 --> 00:04:40.659
could end up being one of the

00:04:40.759 --> 00:04:42.628
best burning mans for a lot of

00:04:42.761 --> 00:04:43.629
people because it used all of

00:04:43.762 --> 00:04:46.398
the principles all at once, and

00:04:46.398 --> 00:04:48.033
tested it for the full

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:48.433
experience.

00:04:48.533 --> 00:04:49.401
&gt;&gt; Yeah, it certainly did test

00:04:49.468 --> 00:04:52.838
you all, and you know, with that

00:04:52.971 --> 00:04:54.940
idea of self-reliance here, that

00:04:55.073 --> 00:04:56.475
is also something that was

00:04:56.642 --> 00:04:56.842
tested.

00:04:56.975 --> 00:04:57.676
But that said, do you think that

00:04:57.843 --> 00:04:58.977
there are things that could have

00:04:59.411 --> 00:05:01.413
been handled better by

00:05:01.413 --> 00:05:01.613
organizers?

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:04.583
What are your thoughts on that?

00:05:04.683 --> 00:05:06.885
&gt;&gt; Actually, so this is the

00:05:06.985 --> 00:05:08.954
first time this has been, you

00:05:09.087 --> 00:05:11.423
know, in 35 years that they've

00:05:11.423 --> 00:05:13.458
been doing this festival, I

00:05:13.558 --> 00:05:15.427
think this is the first time

00:05:15.494 --> 00:05:16.995
that anything like this has

00:05:17.095 --> 00:05:17.429
happened.

00:05:17.496 --> 00:05:21.433
I think they handled it to the

00:05:21.466 --> 00:05:23.435
best of their ability and put

00:05:23.502 --> 00:05:25.103
out all the proper instructions,

00:05:25.437 --> 00:05:30.442
which is not to move.

00:05:30.442 --> 00:05:30.976
Then it was up to the attendees

00:05:31.109 --> 00:05:31.510
to follow those rules.

00:05:31.677 --> 00:05:32.711
As soon as you start moving

00:05:32.878 --> 00:05:36.448
30,000 pound vehicles, rvs,

00:05:36.481 --> 00:05:38.450
things without 4 by 4, you're

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:39.584
going to get stuck, so if you

00:05:39.718 --> 00:05:41.019
listen to the rules, it's all

00:05:41.453 --> 00:05:41.987
drying up right now.

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:44.723
People are starting to leave,

00:05:44.823 --> 00:05:45.457
but the people that started to

00:05:45.557 --> 00:05:47.459
leave and panic or wanted to get

00:05:47.459 --> 00:05:48.727
out ahead of time while it was

00:05:48.827 --> 00:05:51.096
still raining, they're still

00:05:51.463 --> 00:05:51.530
stuck out there.

00:05:51.697 --> 00:05:52.597
They're still stuck out on the

00:05:52.731 --> 00:05:55.467
road out, and they're causing a

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:56.468
bottleneck situation for all of

00:05:56.468 --> 00:05:58.470
the people that actually stayed

00:05:58.603 --> 00:06:00.839
and listened.

00:06:01.006 --> 00:06:01.540
&gt;&gt; So you've stayed, you've

00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:01.907
listened.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:02.641
When are you planning to leave?

00:06:02.741 --> 00:06:05.043
&gt;&gt; I'm listening.

00:06:05.477 --> 00:06:06.845
I'm probably going to leave

00:06:06.945 --> 00:06:10.482
after the man burns tonight or

00:06:10.549 --> 00:06:11.149
tomorrow morning because as you

00:06:11.483 --> 00:06:12.851
guys said, and we've been

00:06:13.018 --> 00:06:15.487
notified that the Gates are now

00:06:15.487 --> 00:06:15.520
open.

00:06:15.654 --> 00:06:17.656
The problem is that this Monday

00:06:17.756 --> 00:06:19.491
is the mass exodus, so this is

00:06:19.491 --> 00:06:21.493
when the traffic will be the

00:06:21.493 --> 00:06:23.495
heaviest, so people can plan on

00:06:23.562 --> 00:06:25.030
sitting in their cars from

00:06:25.163 --> 00:06:29.835
anywhere from two to 12 to 14

00:06:29.968 --> 00:06:30.869
hours on the way out so I'm

00:06:31.036 --> 00:06:32.504
going to wait and hopefully just

00:06:32.504 --> 00:06:33.505
be this line for a couple hours

00:06:33.505 --> 00:06:37.609
before I head to Reno.

00:06:37.776 --> 00:06:39.511
&gt;&gt; Patience is a virtue for

00:06:39.511 --> 00:06:40.545
sure, caz, thank you so much for

00:06:40.679 --> 00:06:41.680
being with us, and we hope that

00:06:41.847 --> 00:06:44.516
you have a wonderful time.

00:06:44.516 --> 00:06:45.984
You're a very optimistic, even

00:06:46.151 --> 00:06:47.519
under these conditions.

00:06:47.586 --> 00:06:50.155
&gt;&gt; It's such a great community

00:06:50.522 --> 00:06:52.190
to be a part of, and it really

